  "facts": [
    {
      "id": "snapshots",
      "claim": "Facade builds, credential resolution and router resolution and recording each read one settings snapshot per operation instead of several config.Get() calls; behavior is unchanged. The unused core.Engine adapter (core_adapter.go), which nothing in production built or served and which was the gateway's only use of the deprecated core.Principal, is removed.",
      "status": "observed",
      "evidence": {
        "source": "go/internal/providers/factory.go and related; go/internal/router/failover.go; removed go/internal/providers/core_adapter.go"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "boundary",
      "claim": "The boundary test now names internal/providers, internal/router and internal/api/transport_mode.go the product adapter layer, records why each still reads settings or iam, and keeps a ratchet that only shrinks (providers 55 iam and 13 config.Get, router 6 and 10, transport_mode 0 and 1). New tests require the three libraries at release tags with no replace directives, and keep retired deprecated core APIs out of the gateway.",
      "status": "observed",
      "evidence": {
        "source": "go/internal/architecture"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "docs",
      "claim": "docs/ARCHITECTURE.md describes the real module graph and ownership: llmgw-core depends on llm-provider-auth and llm-translate and owns the provider verticals, transports, Runtime, catalog service, execution primitives, OAuth flow service and anonymous orchestrator; the gateway owns settings, IAM and stores, routing policy, the console and portal, and the adapters, each named. go/README.md, CONTRIBUTING.md and docs/PROVIDERS.md drop stale statements.",
      "status": "observed",
      "evidence": {
        "source": "docs/ARCHITECTURE.md, go/README.md, CONTRIBUTING.md, docs/PROVIDERS.md; check-docs"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "suite",
      "claim": "The full Go suite passes with HTTP_PROXY and HTTPS_PROXY unreachable with unchanged characterization goldens; gofmt, vet, govulncheck (0 reachable), check-docs and git diff --check pass.",
      "status": "observed",
      "evidence": {
        "source": "local gate run on the reviewed head"
      }
    }
  ],
